WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.720
Correlation connects indicators from different public sources to understand possible relationships.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.500
Domains, subdomains, DNS answers, certificates, internet addresses, providers, repositories,

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.960
packages, websites, and organizations can be arranged in a timeline or relationship map.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.480
Every connection should describe its evidence.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.260
A domain resolved to an address on a date.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.040
A certificate covered a hostname during a validity period.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.400
A repository referenced a domain in a file.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.600
These statements are stronger than a vague line suggesting ownership.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.280
Time prevents false relationships.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:39.160
An address can be reassigned, a certificate can expire, and a vendor can change.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.520
Place observations on a timeline before combining them.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.560
Two indicators observed years apart may not describe the same operational state.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.340
Ownership indicators include official statements, authoritative records, consistent branding,

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.280
repository control, contractual confirmation, and internal inventory.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.540
Each has limitations.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.160
Hosting, naming similarity, or one shared provider rarely proves common control.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.520
Assign confidence based on source quality, independence, consistency,

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.780
and remaining alternatives.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.720
Look for disconfirming evidence and shared-infrastructure explanations.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:12.760
Avoid false attribution, which can waste response effort and harm unrelated parties.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.380
A relationship map is an analytical aid, not proof by appearance.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.840
Keep source identifiers attached to nodes and edges, distinguish observed facts from judgments,

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.460
and report uncertainty so reviewers can challenge or update the model.
